cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "North Pacific Strategy Initiative — Working Papers"
message: >-
  If you cite an individual NPSI working paper, please use the per-paper
  citation metadata embedded in its reading view (the citation_* meta tags
  consumed by Google Scholar and reference managers), or the GitHub release
  tag for that paper. For the imprint itself, please use the citation below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jesse
    family-names: James
    email: editor@npsi.ca
    affiliation: North Pacific Strategy Initiative
abstract: >-
  The North Pacific Strategy Initiative is an independent research imprint
  publishing reference-grade working papers on Pacific sovereignty, bilateral
  financial architecture, and the defensive options available to middle powers
  in a period of dollar-system stress.
keywords:
  - Pacific sovereignty
  - bilateral architecture
  - middle-power policy
  - Canada
  - Korea
  - counterparty-risk diversification
url: "https://npsi.ca/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cherishwins/npsi-site"
license: CC-BY-4.0
